    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Cego',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cego: German Tarock from Baden; 3–4p, 54-card Cego deck (22 trumps + 32 in 4 suits). Central hand (Legage/Cego); many contracts use Legage. Developed from Ombre and Dreierles. Two-phase bidding; declarer may play from Cego (central hand); follow suit, must trump if unable to follow; 70 card points total, bidder needs 36+ to win normal contracts.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Germany (Baden, Hohenzollern). Cego developed early 19th c. from Dreierles and Ombre (Napoleonic Wars). 54-card Cego deck; central hand (Legage). National game of Baden; only German region where genuine Tarok cards remain in general use.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3â€“4. Individual or partnerships by contract.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '54-card Cego deck (22 trumps Trocke + 8 per suit).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cego deck; score sheet.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Varies by contract; central hand (Legage) dealt; many contracts use Legage. Anticlockwise.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Pflicht-Räuber: Compulsory round of Räuber at fixed time (e.g. 23:00); one deal per player, no other bidding. Loser pays; if one player takes no tricks loser pays 60; stakes multiply after the round.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Ministranten Version: Bräunlingen variant: Vorhand can choose Cego, Piccolo, Bettel, Geregelter Räuber, Wilder Räuber or Dresch when all pass. Stricter rules for Eine Leere / Zwei Leere (must lead exposed cards; bidder leads after first trick(s)).',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
